# Per-package coverage floors, enforced by scripts/check-coverage.sh in CI.
#
# A single repo-wide average lets a well-covered package mask an untested one: the
# gate this replaced measured only ./pkg/..., which is 111 lines, and reported 90%
# while the packages holding money, credentials, and the live-mode guardrails went
# unmeasured. Floors are per package and ratchet upward only.
#
# Raise a floor when you raise its coverage. Never lower one to make CI pass.
#
# A floor may be re-measured, not lowered, when the toolchain changes how it counts
# statements. Go 1.27 instruments more statements per function than 1.25 did: with an
# unchanged test suite, internal/gen moved 11.7% -> 9.7% and internal/moneycheck
# 16.0% -> 15.5%, while config, diagnostics, docgen and transport rose. No test was
# lost. The two floors below carry their 1.27 measurement and the date, so the next
# reader can tell a re-measurement from a regression.
#
# Go 1.27.3 counts a multi-value assignment (`a, b := f()`) as one statement where
# 1.27.0 counted one per name, and a map composite literal as one where 1.27.0 counted
# two. Blocks and their hits are identical between the two; only the statement weights
# changed. internal/config went 114 -> 109 statements (98 -> 93 covered) and
# internal/diagnostics 50 -> 48 (28 -> 26), every dropped statement a covered one.
#
# The money, credential, and safety-gate packages (cli, config, transport, output,
# apperr, redact, permissions, api) are held at the 85% target and marked below.
# internal/update joined them when `lago upgrade` stopped self-installing: it no longer
# downloads a binary, but it is now the code that tells an operator how to upgrade.
# The remaining packages are code generators and doc tooling: a defect there fails
# `make generate-check` visibly rather than moving money, so they carry today's
# measured value as a ratchet floor instead of the 85% bar.

# --- money, credentials, safety gates: 85% target ---------------------------
internal/apperr         94.0
internal/cli            86.0
internal/config         85.0   # re-measured on Go 1.27.3, 2026-11-03 (was 86.0 on Go 1.27.0)
internal/output         97.0
internal/permissions   100.0
internal/redact        100.0
internal/transport      93.0
internal/update         82.0
pkg/api                 90.0

# --- generators and tooling: ratchet floors ---------------------------------
internal/diagnostics    54.0   # re-measured on Go 1.27.3, 2026-11-03 (was 56.0 on Go 1.27.0)
internal/docgen         58.0
internal/gen            59.0   # raised 2026-11-10 with the API v2 generator tests (was 9.5)
internal/generated     100.0   # raised 2026-11-10 when the table decode moved into a tested helper
internal/moneycheck     15.0  # re-measured on Go 1.27, 2026-09-01 (was 16.0 on Go 1.25)
